# results/figures/ holds the retired pre-B1 headline chart. `headline_auroc.json` and
# `headline_auroc.png` are TRACKED (they predate this rule and tracking beats ignoring), so a
# cloner gets them and gets a clean AUROC of 1.000 with nothing beside it saying that the 1.000
# is the selection rule rather than the detector. Their retirement notices therefore have to
# ship too, and git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded -- so this is
# `results/figures/*`, matching the contents, and not `results/figures/`, matching the directory.
# Ignoring a retirement notice is the same defect as writing no notice at all (see the
# `!results/*.SUPERSEDED.json` rule below, which is the same argument for checkpoints).
results/figures/*
!results/figures/README.md
!results/figures/*.SUPERSEDED.json
results/runs/
results/samples/
!results/.gitkeep
!results/*.md
!results/env_check.txt

